{
  "cell": "ro_nand2_wstv0p48",
  "_comment": [
    "Cell descriptor for layout/bin/compose-cell.py -- see layout/README.md",
    "section 'Composing a gate' for the floorplan reasoning shared with every",
    "other cell, and layout/ro_nand2/README.md for this cell's own result.",
    "",
    "ro_nand2 is design/ro_array_core.spice's per-ring NAND2 stage (the",
    "enable-gated first stage of each ro_ring5): a parallel PMOS pull-up pair",
    "(Mpa/Mpb, gates a/en) and a series NMOS pull-down pair (Mna/Mnb, gates",
    "a/en) between the same starve-device pair ro_stage uses (Mph/Mnt,",
    "cross-coupled to the OPPOSITE rail exactly as in ro_stage). Six devices",
    "total -- the same cross-coupled-starve-gate shape as ro_stage, reusing",
    "its two-pass 'stages' technique directly, plus two new floorplan moves:",
    "",
    "1. Mna/Mnb (series: XMna y a nm / XMnb nm en ny) are drawn as ONE",
    "   mos_array call with fingers=2, finger_topology='series' -- the",
    "   generator chains two fingers source-to-drain on one shared internal",
    "   diffusion segment (reported as U0_S0/U0_D0/U0_S1, D0 being the",
    "   internal shared node), so the 'nm' net needs no external wire at all:",
    "   it is already one physical node by construction. U0_S0=ny, U0_G0=en,",
    "   U0_D0=nm (left unconnected -- internal), U0_G1=a, U0_S1=y.",
    "2. Mpa/Mpb (parallel: both XMpa/XMpb have D=y, S=py) are drawn as TWO",
    "   separate mos_array calls (both pfet_w0p84_l0p15), Mpa 'mirror_y' and",
    "   Mpb 'rotate_180' -- the rotate_180 flip makes Mpb's own D face LEFT",
    "   (toward Mpa's D) so the two drains land at the SAME y with a 0.62 um",
    "   direct gap (identical technique to Mph/Mp's 'py' short in ro_stage),",
    "   while Mpb's S ends up on the cell's far east edge, facing away.",
    "   Merging Mpa's nwell into Mpb's (0.10 um bbox overlap, same technique",
    "   as Mph/Mp) keeps the whole PMOS row -- Mph+Mpa+Mpb -- on one",
    "   physical nwell needing only Mph's own tap.",
    "",
    "Both of the above create THREE-way nets (py: Mph.D+Mpa.S+Mpb.S; y:",
    "Mpa.D+Mpb.D+Mna.D) whose 'far' leg cannot be wired in the base stage: a",
    "straight run from either far pin re-crosses another of the row's own",
    "S/D pads (a same-block self-net pad-crossing once stage 'core' becomes",
    "one composed block). So stage 'core' promotes EVERY py/y endpoint",
    "(mph_py/mpa_py/mpb_py, mpa_y/mpb_y/mnab_y) as bare pins -- wiring",
    "neither net inside stage 'core' at all -- alongside ro_stage's usual",
    "mph_g/mnt_g cross-coupled-gate promotion, and the final stage resolves",
    "all six same-block self-net legs on metal2 in one gen-compose call (so",
    "the router's own route-vs-route check sees all six lanes at once):",
    "py's two legs, y's two legs, and ro_stage's usual vss/vddr pair.",
    "Every waypoint lane was chosen empirically (see README) to give each",
    "leg clearance from the OTHER five legs' own known pad positions -- the",
    "route-vs-route collision check treats 'core's own promoted ports as the",
    "only known obstacles once ro_stage's per-sub-block visibility is gone,",
    "so a lane merely needs to skip the pads it is not addressing, not every",
    "sub-block's individual bbox.",
    "",
    "VARIANT NOTE (issue #22/#27): this is the wstv=0.48 starve-width",
    "instance -- design/ro_array_core.spice's ring xr4 --",
    "identical topology/floorplan to the wstv=0.42 (ring xr1) cell this",
    "was cloned from, with exactly two changes: Mph/Mnt's own w_um param,",
    "and their placement.origins_um.y, re-derived from the closed-form",
    "layout/README.md documents ('Starve-width variants' section):",
    "  mph_oy(w) = 3.74 + w/2",
    "  mnt_oy(w) = 0.21 - w/2",
    "(w/2 is mos_array's own reported S/D-pad local y for an l_um=2",
    "starve device at width w -- empirically linear across 0.42-0.48um,",
    "identical for both flavors -- so this keeps Mph/Mp's 'py' merge and",
    "Mnt/Mn's 'ny' route at the exact same absolute y the wstv=0.42 cell",
    "used, which is what py/ny's straight (no-jog) routes depend on.",
    "Every other block/origin/waypoint is untouched from the wstv=0.42",
    "cell.json this was cloned from."
  ],
